tion and hold; overhead arm action is a variant or cue, not a new primary movement.","distinguishingDimensions":{"armAction":"overhead_reach_then_forceful_snap"}},{"name":"Supported Drop Squat to Stick","classification":"new_variant","rationale":"Light external support reduces balance demand while preserving the non-jump bilateral landing pattern.","distinguishingDimensions":{"supportLevel":"light_external_support"}},{"name":"Single-Leg Drop Squat to Stick","classification":"new_variant","rationale":"Unilateral stance materially increases frontal-plane and balance demand while retaining a non-jump rapid landing shape.","distinguishingDimensions":{"laterality":"unilateral"}},{"name":"Drop Squat to Vertical Jump","classification":"new_definition","rationale":"Adding an immediate maximal takeoff changes the primary stimulus from landing-position acquisition to explosive force production.","distinguishingDimensions":{"primaryTrainingStimulus":"vertical_power","reboundIntent":"immediate_takeoff"}},{"name":"Low Box Drop to Stick","classification":"new_variant","rationale":"External height increases gravitational landing load and equipment constraints but preserves the force-attenuation pattern.","distinguishingDimensions":{"surfaceHeight":"low_box","startPosition":"elevated_step_off"}}]}$card_1_payload$::JSONB);
